WEBVTT

00:01:27.385 --> 00:01:30.514
But she didn't have
enough money for an Uber,

00:01:30.538 --> 00:01:33.183
and she didn't have
another friend to call.

00:01:33.858 --> 00:01:35.570
But she did have me,

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:38.599
and I was able to get her
another appointment,

00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:40.953
which she kept without difficulty.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.337
She wasn't resistant,

00:01:43.361 --> 00:01:45.201
it's just that her ride didn't show.

00:01:46.669 --> 00:01:50.588
I wish I could say that this
was an isolated incident,

00:01:50.612 --> 00:01:53.638
but I know from running
the safety net systems

00:01:53.662 --> 00:01:58.247
in San Francisco, Los Angeles,
and now New York City,

00:01:59.181 --> 00:02:02.779
that health care is built
on a middle-class model